  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I use tiny avatars a lot. I put a lot of time into making sure the scale of everything I create feels right. One thing I'd love to be able to do is to have the option to select a friend (or any user who allows me to interact with them via avatar dynamics) and find a bone or object on their avatar that I can anchor myself to with a chair. This way, I could sit on my friend's heads, shoulders, or anything else and get carried around as they move. As someone who uses tiny avatars, this would be immensely helpful for things like cuddling, not getting lost in a conversation because people can't see me, and in a lot of instances, keeping my head above the water in worlds with pools or hot tubs.\nIt would also be immensely fun to sit on a springjoint and get flung around, but I'm weird.",
